# Documents that are internal by nature, wherever they sit. The directory rules
# above cover the normal case; these catch a strategy/incident note that gets
# written into docs/ by mistake. Enforced (not just hinted) by
# tests/private-boundary.test.js — .gitignore is bypassable with `git add -f`,
# a test that reads `git ls-files` is not.
*.private.md
internal-*.md
*-internal.md
